# Help Desk Ticketing

I set up Spiceworks Cloud Help Desk and used the ticketing system to create, manage and resolve support tickets.

## Help Desk Setup

I set up my help desk and added users and technicians so I could create and manage support requests.

[SCREENSHOT]

My Spiceworks help desk and ticket queue.

## Creating Support Tickets

I created tickets for different IT issues that could come up while supporting users. I included information about the problem so the issue could be tracked from when it was reported.

[SCREENSHOT]

Support tickets created in Spiceworks.

## Assigning and Managing Tickets

I assigned tickets to a technician and worked with the priority and status depending on the issue. I also reassigned a ticket when the problem needed to be handled at a different support level.

[SCREENSHOT]

A support ticket showing the assignee, priority and status.

## Ticket Notes and Responses

While working on tickets, I added notes and responses to keep a record of what was checked and what had already been done.

[SCREENSHOT]

Notes and updates documented on a support ticket.

## Resolving and Closing Tickets

After an issue was finished, I added the resolution and closed the ticket. This kept a record of the problem and what was done to fix it.

[SCREENSHOT]

A resolved support ticket with the final notes.

## Reopening a Ticket

I reopened a closed ticket to work through what would happen if a user reported that the same issue came back.

[SCREENSHOT]

A previously closed ticket reopened for additional work.
